  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Commits, Refs & The Graph",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What A Commit Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Immutable object: tree + parent(s) + author + committer + message",
            "tree SHA is a FULL snapshot, never a delta",
            "Change one byte of any field and the hash changes",
            "A diff is computed on demand between two trees"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git cat-file -p HEAD",
            "tree 9f2a1c...   # whole snapshot",
            "parent 4c1b0e... # 0, 1 or 2+ of these",
            "author Ada <a@x> 1772... +0530"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every integration command is graph surgery plus tree comparison. Nothing else."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Refs Are Just Pointers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A branch is a 41-byte file holding one SHA",
            "Creating a branch is O(1) — no copying",
            "HEAD is a symbolic ref pointing at a branch",
            "Detached HEAD = HEAD holds a raw commit SHA"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ cat .git/refs/heads/main",
            "a1b2c3d4e5...    # 40 hex + newline",
            "$ cat .git/HEAD",
            "ref: refs/heads/main   # symbolic"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Parent Count = Kind",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Parents",
            "Kind",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "0",
              "root",
              "first commit"
            ],
            [
              "1",
              "normal",
              "linear history"
            ],
            [
              "2+",
              "merge",
              "HEAD^1 / HEAD^2"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Ancestry & Merge Base",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git merge-base --is-ancestor A B  # exit 0",
            "git merge-base main feature   # fork point",
            "# ancestor? -> fast-forward. else 3-way."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Merge base = best common ancestor of two tips",
            "That one ancestry test picks the whole algorithm",
            "`git log --graph` draws the same topology"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Range Syntax",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Syntax",
            "Means",
            "Reads as"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "main..feature",
              "in B not A",
              "what the PR adds"
            ],
            [
              "main...feature",
              "symmetric diff",
              "both divergences"
            ],
            [
              "feature..main",
              "behind by",
              "what you missed"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config merge.conflictStyle zdiff3",
            "# adds the ||||||| base section",
            "# set --global; never guess intent again"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Reflog: The Undo Log",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Records every move of HEAD and branch tips",
            "Kept ~90 days; entries addressable as HEAD@{n}",
            "Survives rebase, reset, checkout, bad merges"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Fast-Forward: Pointer Motion Only",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Identity Rule",
          "text": "Commit identity = content + parents + metadata. Replay a commit on a new base and the SHA MUST change, even if the diff is byte-identical."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Exact Condition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Current tip is an ancestor of the branch merged in",
            "No divergence, so nothing to reconcile",
            "No merge base needed; conflict is impossible"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "C1",
              "C2 = main",
              "C3",
              "C4 = feature",
              "main ref jumps to C4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Pointer Motion Only",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git checkout main      # main sits at C2",
            "git merge feature      # main -> C4",
            "# no new object; refs/heads/main rewritten"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cost: O(1) ref write plus checkout of changed files",
            "History stays a straight line",
            "Zero new objects are created"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Flags That Pick Shape",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Behaviour",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "default",
              "ff when possible",
              "everyday sync"
            ],
            [
              "--ff-only",
              "fails loudly",
              "CI gates, scripts"
            ],
            [
              "--no-ff",
              "forces merge commit",
              "keep the bubble"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Config The Default",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config merge.ff only  # no implicit merges",
            "git config pull.ff only   # safe git pull",
            "# set --global once, stop thinking about it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. What You Trade",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Linear history is clean and trivially bisectable",
            "But it erases the fact a branch ever existed",
            "--no-ff keeps a visible topic-branch bubble",
            "Choose per branch, not per mood"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Platform Buttons",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "GitHub button",
            "Produces",
            "Linear?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Rebase and merge",
              "replayed commits",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "Squash and merge",
              "one commit",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "Create merge commit",
              "two parents",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Two-way diff cannot do this: without BASE, 'they added a line' and 'we deleted a line' look identical. BASE supplies intent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Three-Way Merge & The ort Strategy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Read The Ref, Not The Log",
          "items": [
            "Before: cat .git/refs/heads/main",
            "git merge feature",
            "After: same file, new SHA",
            "That is the entire operation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Quiet Gotcha",
          "text": "A fast-forward discards nothing, but it also runs no merge driver and creates no merge commit — hooks or tooling keyed on merge commits silently never fire."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. When It Is Needed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Both branches gained commits since the merge base",
            "Histories diverged, so pointer motion is impossible",
            "Git must reconcile two sets of edits, not pick one"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Three Inputs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Input",
            "Tree",
            "Is"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "BASE",
              "merge base",
              "common ancestor"
            ],
            [
              "OURS",
              "HEAD",
              "branch you are on"
            ],
            [
              "THEIRS",
              "MERGE_HEAD",
              "branch merged in"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Per-Hunk Rule",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Changed vs BASE",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ours only",
              "take ours"
            ],
            [
              "theirs only",
              "take theirs"
            ],
            [
              "both, identically",
              "take it once"
            ],
            [
              "both, differently",
              "conflict"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Merge Commit",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git show HEAD^1   # branch you were on",
            "git show HEAD^2   # branch you merged in",
            "git log --first-parent main  # integrations"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two parents; first-parent order is not cosmetic",
            "--first-parent hides all intra-feature noise",
            "Useful only if you merge consistently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Strategy: ort",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default since Git 2.34, replacing `recursive`",
            "Faster, fewer edge cases, better rename handling",
            "Criss-cross history yields multiple merge bases",
            "ort merges those bases into one virtual base"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Renames Are Inferred",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Git records no renames — it guesses by similarity",
            "Default threshold 50%; tune with -M (e.g. -M40%)",
            "Below threshold: edits do not follow the file"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What It Computes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git switch feature",
            "git rebase main   # replays main..feature",
            "# each commit re-applied on main's tip"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Rebase: Replay Onto A New Base",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Strategy Options",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Option",
            "Scope",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "-X ours",
              "conflicting hunks",
              "prefer our side"
            ],
            [
              "-X theirs",
              "conflicting hunks",
              "prefer their side"
            ],
            [
              "-s ours",
              "whole merge",
              "drop their content"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Cost Model",
          "text": "Roughly O(changed files) with per-file diff cost; the graph walk to find the base is near-linear in commits since divergence. Branch size, not repo size."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Take the commits in `main..feature`",
            "Re-apply each in order on top of main",
            "Result is linear: as if written on latest main",
            "No merge commit is created"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. New SHAs, Always",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same tree, different parent, therefore different hash",
            "Old commits become unreachable, not modified",
            "They live in the reflog until it expires"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Internals",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "checkout new base (detached)",
              "cherry-pick commit 1..n",
              "move branch ref to result",
              "old tip left in reflog"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. --onto Transplant",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rebase --onto main topicA topicB",
            "# form: --onto NEWBASE UPSTREAM BRANCH",
            "# lifts topicB off topicA onto main"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Conflicts Repeat",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Resolved per replayed commit, not once",
            "A 10-commit rebase can show one conflict 10 times",
            "rerere caches resolutions and replays them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config --global rerere.enabled true",
            "# reuse recorded resolution, per conflict hunk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Control Verbs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "When",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "--continue",
              "after git add",
              "next commit"
            ],
            [
              "--skip",
              "commit is junk",
              "drop it"
            ],
            [
              "--abort",
              "gone wrong",
              "exact restore"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Rebasing Your Pull",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git pull --rebase   # no merge bubble",
            "git config pull.rebase true  # permanent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git cherry-pick 9f2a1c      # one commit",
            "git cherry-pick main~4..main~1  # a range",
            "git cherry-pick -n a1b2     # stage only"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That is exactly why a cherry-pick can conflict — it is never a blind patch application."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cherry-Pick, Patch-IDs & Revert",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Cost & Recovery",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "O(n) cherry-picks for n commits, linear",
            "Each pick pays a full three-way merge cost",
            "Pre-rebase tip is in reflog as HEAD@{n}",
            "`git reset --hard ORIG_HEAD` undoes a finished rebase"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Rebase's Atom",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Applies C's diff (vs C's parent) onto HEAD",
            "Creates a brand new commit with a new SHA",
            "Rebase is essentially a loop over cherry-pick"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. It Is A Three-Way Merge",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Role",
            "Tree"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "BASE",
              "C's parent"
            ],
            [
              "OURS",
              "HEAD"
            ],
            [
              "THEIRS",
              "C"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Stage, Then Squash",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-n` / `--no-commit` leaves changes staged",
            "Pick several, commit once, one clean unit",
            "Ranges are exclusive of the left endpoint"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Tracking Backports",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git cherry-pick -x 9f2a1c",
            "# message gains:",
            "# (cherry picked from commit 9f2a1c...)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Patch-ID",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hash of the normalised diff of a commit",
            "Ignores line numbers and whitespace",
            "Recognises 'same change, different SHA'",
            "Rebase drops picks whose patch-id is upstream"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Detect Duplicates",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git cherry -v main feature  # '+' = not upstream",
            "git log --cherry-mark main...feature"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Duplicate Hazard",
          "text": "Cherry-pick from a branch, then later merge that branch: the same change arrives twice and yields spurious conflicts. Prefer merging the source once."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Revert: The Inverse",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Applies the reverse diff as a NEW commit",
            "Adds history instead of rewriting it",
            "Therefore safe on shared branches",
            "Re-rebasing a merged branch is usually a no-op"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Interactive Rebase: The Todo List",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Todo List",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rebase -i HEAD~5   # oldest line first",
            "pick   a1b2 add parser",
            "fixup  c3d4 typo",
            "reword e5f6 bad subject"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Edit verbs, save, Git executes top to bottom",
            "Reordering the lines reorders the commits",
            "Deleting a line deletes the commit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Core Verbs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Verb",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pick",
              "keep as is"
            ],
            [
              "reword",
              "new message only"
            ],
            [
              "edit",
              "stop to amend/split"
            ],
            [
              "drop",
              "remove commit"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Folding & Halting",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Verb",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "squash",
              "fold up, merge messages"
            ],
            [
              "fixup",
              "fold up, drop message"
            ],
            [
              "exec cmd",
              "run shell after point"
            ],
            [
              "break",
              "stop and inspect"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Splitting A Commit",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# mark the commit `edit`, then:",
            "git reset HEAD^        # undo, keep files",
            "git add -p; git commit # in pieces",
            "git rebase --continue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Review-Feedback Loop",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git commit --fixup=a1b2c3",
            "git rebase -i --autosquash main",
            "# fixup auto-parks under its target"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Bisect A Whole Branch",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rebase -i --exec 'npm test' main",
            "# runs tests after EVERY commit",
            "# halts on the first commit that breaks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Reaching The Root",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git rebase -i --root` includes the very first commit",
            "Lets you reword or split the initial commit",
            "Rewrites the entire history hash chain"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Stacked Branches",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--update-refs` (2.38+) drags dependent branch tips",
            "Without it, stacked branches point at dead commits",
            "Set rebase.updateRefs=true to make it default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Downstream Rewrite",
          "text": "Every commit from the edited point onward gets a new SHA — even the ones you never touched — because their parent changed. Rewrite depth is measured from the earliest edit."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Index Has Stages",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git ls-files -u src/app.ts",
            "100644 <sha> 1 src/app.ts   # base",
            "100644 <sha> 2 src/app.ts   # ours",
            "100644 <sha> 3 src/app.ts   # theirs"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Conflicts: Anatomy & Fixes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A conflicted path holds 3 entries, not 1",
            "Staging the path collapses it back to stage 0",
            "That collapse is what 'resolved' means"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Marker Anatomy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "<<<<<<< HEAD        # ours",
            "||||||| merged ancestor   # diff3 only",
            "=======             # theirs below",
            ">>>>>>> feature"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Labels Invert",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operation",
            "OURS is",
            "THEIRS is"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "merge",
              "your branch",
              "incoming branch"
            ],
            [
              "rebase",
              "upstream base",
              "your own commit"
            ],
            [
              "cherry-pick",
              "HEAD",
              "picked commit"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "During rebase you are replaying onto upstream, so upstream is 'ours'. This single inversion causes most backwards resolutions."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Tree Conflicts",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "modify/delete, rename/rename, rename/modify, add/add",
            "Structural — no marker text exists to edit",
            "Decide with `git rm` or `git add`, explicitly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Take One Whole Side",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git checkout --ours   conf.yml",
            "git checkout --theirs conf.yml",
            "git checkout --merge  conf.yml  # redo markers"
